#!/bin/sh
# Edemint Pi firstboot: grow the root partition to fill the SD/NVMe and
# resize the ext4 filesystem to match. Idempotent via /var/lib/edemint/
# firstboot-grown stamp; the unit also gates on that path.
set -eu

STAMP=/var/lib/edemint/firstboot-grown
mkdir -p "$(dirname "$STAMP")"
[ -e "$STAMP" ] && exit 0

ROOT_SRC="$(findmnt -no SOURCE /)"          # e.g. /dev/mmcblk0p2
ROOT_DEV="$(lsblk -no PKNAME "$ROOT_SRC")"  # e.g. mmcblk0
ROOT_PART_NUM="$(echo "$ROOT_SRC" | sed 's|.*[^0-9]||')"

# Grow the partition then the filesystem. parted prints a warning when
# the partition isn't aligned; tolerate it.
parted -s "/dev/$ROOT_DEV" resizepart "$ROOT_PART_NUM" 100% || true
partprobe "/dev/$ROOT_DEV" || true
resize2fs "$ROOT_SRC"

touch "$STAMP"
echo "edemint-firstboot: root grown to fill device."
